dropbear
Usage: dropbear [-r hostkey] [-p [ADDR:]PORT] [-s] [-w] [-F] [-E]

The ssh SERVER. On vos it is the one listening service, it accepts only
public-key logins (no passwords), and init binds it to the wireguard
interface alone -- so it is reachable through your tunnel and invisible
on the untrusted network the stick is plugged into.

	-r FILE		host key file (ed25519)
	-p ADDR:PORT	listen only on this address and port
	-s		disable password logins (already off in this build)
	-w		disable root password logins
	-F		run in the foreground, do not fork
	-E		log to stderr rather than the system log
	-g		disable password logins for root

	dropbear -r /state/ssh_host_key -p 10.9.0.1:22 -s -F -E

A host key committed to a reproducible public image would be a published
private key, so vos generates its host key on the encrypted state
partition the first time you set remote access up.

See also: dropbearkey, dbclient, wg
